module test.claim.long.host_identity_single_authoring_witness_test

import v2.std.decl_index { DataDeclTypeFact, data_decl_type_facts }
import v2.std.live_tree { LiveTreeDisposition, SubstrateInputsOnly }
import std.types { String, List, Int, Bool }

data live_tree_disposition: LiveTreeDisposition = SubstrateInputsOnly

// WHAT THIS WITNESS ESTABLISHES, AND IT IS DELIBERATELY NARROWER THAN ITS NAME SUGGESTS TO A READER
// WHO DOES NOT READ THIS BLOCK. It asserts that gunbc.fleet_physical_inventory declares NO data of
// type HostIdentity -- that one module has stopped being a second authoring surface for an identity
// gunbc.fleet_intent_network already owns. It is RED before the deletion that lands with it (six
// such rows) and green after, which is what makes it evidence rather than decoration.
//
// IT DOES NOT ESTABLISH THAT HOST IDENTITY IS AUTHORED ONCE IN THE CORPUS, and the difference
// matters enough to state before anyone cites it. Measured 2026-08-22 by executing the reflection
// surface: 26 data declarations in the tree are typed HostIdentity. Most are legitimate -- witness
// fixtures, single-host subjects, and gunbc.ci_fleet gunbc_ci_host_identity, which authors an
// entirely different host ("gunbc-ci-fleet"). A corpus-wide uniqueness claim would be false, and
// asserting it would be the carrier claiming more than its evidence entails.
//
// TWO POPULATIONS THIS WITNESS STRUCTURALLY CANNOT REACH, named so the gap is on the record rather
// than papered over by a green check that looks broader than it is:
//
// ONE -- ROSTERS THAT ESCAPE THE TYPE. gunbc.fleet_reach_endpoint fleet_reach_probe_targets is a
// hand-authored six-element list of bare Strings naming the same six hosts, with four production
// consumers. No assertion over HostIdentity declarations can ever see it, because it never engages
// the type. This is the sharp form of the branding point: the problem is not that the brand is
// weak, it is that NOTHING REQUIRES THE BRAND TO BE USED, so a fork can simply decline to be typed.
//
// TWO -- VALUES, AS OPPOSED TO DECLARATIONS. The honest claim one would want is that no two
// declarations author the same host STRING, which would also correctly permit
// gunbc.host_standup srv3_host_standup_target, since that REFERENCES operator_host_srv3 rather than
// re-authoring "srv3". That claim is not expressible today: v2.std.decl_index DataDeclTypeFact
// carries no value, and the DeclFact initializer projection reports the same kind
// (DataInitializerTypecheckedSubjectAbsentProjection) for a string literal and for a reference to
// another declaration -- verified by execution against all three specimens, not assumed. So a
// literal-versus-reference discriminator does not exist at this surface.
//
// THE VALUE-GRAIN CEILING, STATED AS A CEILING SO THE NEXT PERSON FINDS THE ANSWER RATHER THAN THE
// WALL. Identity-fork detection at VALUE grain is not available to anyone in this substrate today,
// and no amount of care in specifying a witness reaches it -- the reflection surface simply does not
// carry declaration values. Its trigger is therefore substrate work, not lane work: a reflection
// surface whose declaration facts carry the initializer's value, or at minimum discriminate a
// literal from a reference. Until that exists, "is this host authored twice" is answerable only by a
// human reading two files, and the corpus cannot check it.
//
// NEXT-RUNG TRIGGER FOR THIS WITNESS'S OWN CLASS, and it is not "widen this witness": the class closes when host identity has ONE
// AUTHORING SURFACE THAT A STRING LIST CANNOT BYPASS. That is a different and larger change than
// deduplicating two declarations, and until it lands this class sits at mitigatable -- one module
// is walled by an executing assertion and the rest of the corpus is review diligence.
// WHERE THIS WITNESS EXECUTES, AND THE HONEST ANSWER IS NOWHERE IN CI — a declared rung drop
// (DESIGN §4b(3)), stated on the carrier so it is not rediscovered by the next reader who takes the
// green PR as evidence the assertion ran. It was authored in the fast lane, where it was
// BUDGET-REFUSED and went UNDECIDED: the floor refused rather than passing an undecided row, which
// is the fail-closed arm working. Moved here on the measurement recorded in gunbc.ci_layer_roots
// (its own exclusion row), which is where the numbers live rather than duplicated in this block.
//
// BUT test/claim/long/ IS A HOME, NOT A RUNNER. Measured 2026-08-22: .github/workflows/ holds three
// workflows (witnesses, fleet-converge, fleet-desired) and none invokes a long lane or a falsifier
// cadence — DESIGN's CI entry already lists the falsifier cadence among what the floor cut left
// unguarded. The floor's own counters say the same thing from the other side: declined_long=543
// sites are DISCOVERED AND NEVER RUN. So this witness is counted, located, hand-runnable by the
// recipe on its exclusion row, and executed by nothing on a cadence.
//
// DO NOT SIZE THE ROSTER GAP FROM THE NUMBER ABOVE — IT IS THE SMALLER OF THE TWO DECLINE ARMS, and
// this block would otherwise be the exact place a reader picks up the wrong denominator. Admission
// is an OR of two independent arms, not one gate: a long home declines first, then a live-tree read
// declines second. Measured on this branch's own floor run 32582755530 (head 8b28945b27, so the base
// is stated rather than inherited): declined_long=543 and declined_live=830. The live arm is the
// LARGER population by half again, and the corpus already says so about itself in
// test.claim.transport_script_wall_compile_red_test, which recorded 766 against 536 at its own
// measurement and observed that an entire multi-session effort had been aimed at the smaller arm.
// This lane did the same thing. Anyone sizing the gap starts from the live arm.
//
// AND ADMISSION TESTS THE AUTHORED MODULE NAME, NOT THE FILE PATH — required_floor matches the
// module declaration against long_home_prefixes ("test.claim.long."), which is why this file's move
// renamed its module in the same commit. The corollary is the one that misleads: moving a module OUT
// of the long prefix is NOT an admission, it just re-decides which arm declines it. Measured at
// identity grain by the transport_script witness — declined_long 539->536, declined_live 763->766,
// the same three identities, never Planned.
//
// PREVIOUS RUNG: mitigatable, and only ever that — one module walled by an executing assertion while
// the rest of the corpus stayed review diligence. TEMPORARY RUNG: outside the ladder, because an
// unexecuted check establishes nothing at all. REASON: a corpus-scale reflection cost with no lane
// that both admits it and runs it. BOUNDED POPULATION: this file's two witnesses, and it joins an
// existing population rather than opening one — the exclusion row above it covers sixteen more of
// the same class. RESTORATION TRIGGER: a cadence that executes test/claim/long/, or the decl_facts
// surface becoming cheap enough for per-PR discovery, at which point this file moves back and both
// exclusion rows delete together.
//
// WHAT IS NOT CLAIMED: that moving it fixed anything. The deletion this witness was authored to
// evidence still landed and is still correct; what changed is that the evidence no longer runs, and
// saying so here is the difference between a declared drop and coverage by illusion (DESIGN §6).
fn host_identity_data_declarations() -> List<DataDeclTypeFact> {
  filter(
    data_decl_type_facts(pool_roots: ["dag", "src/v2"]),
    f => f.type_name == "HostIdentity",
  )
}

fn host_identity_declarations_in(module_path: String) -> List<DataDeclTypeFact> {
  filter(host_identity_data_declarations(), f => f.module_path == module_path)
}

test fn the_physical_inventory_authors_no_host_identity() -> Bool {
  length(host_identity_declarations_in(module_path: "gunbc.fleet_physical_inventory")) == 0
}

// The positive control, and it is the half that keeps the assertion above from passing vacuously.
// If the reflection surface returned nothing at all -- wrong pool roots, a renamed type, a scan that
// silently found no modules -- the assertion above would be green for the wrong reason and would
// stay green forever. This one fails in that case, because it demands that the surface still SEES
// the authority: gunbc.fleet_intent_network must declare its six.
test fn the_intent_network_still_authors_the_six() -> Bool {
  length(host_identity_declarations_in(module_path: "gunbc.fleet_intent_network")) == 6
}
